## WatchfulEye V3 — Operating Rules (must follow)

### Prime directive
Ship V3 **without breaking** the existing UI and production surfaces. Everything is contract-first, flag-guarded, and auditable.

### Workstream boundaries (no conflicts)
- Every branch/PR maps to exactly **one** workstream slice (WS0..WS12).
- If the task needs contract changes, route them through **WS0** and avoid drive-by edits across the repo.
- Avoid editing shared “hot” files unless explicitly required; prefer new, owned files/dirs per workstream.

### Feature flags (default OFF)
- Any new surface must be behind a `V3_*` flag and default OFF.
- Never remove or regress **Main News Feed**, **Custom News Feed**, **Telegram Intel Reports**, **Intel Reports**, or the **AI Analysis Modal**.

### CodeRabbit workflow (PR-only; no local pre-push gate)
- CodeRabbit runs on **pull requests** via the GitHub app/checks.
- Do **not** block pushes on CodeRabbit CLI auth (headless servers often fail secure credential storage).
- Treat **CodeRabbit + CI + approval** as merge gates (not email).

### Push/PR discipline (agents must finish the loop)
- For any code/doc change:
  - Commit on a correctly named branch (`wsX/*`, `infra/*`, `docs/*`, `fix/*`).
  - Push branch to origin.
  - Open a PR using the repo template and fill the required sections (briefly).
- No direct pushes to `master`.

### Branch creation note (worktree-aware)
- Because `master` is checked out in the staging worktree, in `/opt/watchfuleye2` create new branches from `origin/master`:
  - `git fetch origin master && git checkout -b wsX/<slice> origin/master`

### Staging deploy discipline (must be followed)
- **Two working directories** (never deploy staging from your dev workspace):
  - **Dev workspace**: `/opt/watchfuleye2` (you create branches here and do all work here)
  - **Staging deploy worktree**: `/opt/watchfuleye2-staging` (must track `origin/master` only)
- **Worktree rule**: staging pulls from `master` worktree and restarts staging services; dev workspace stays on feature branches.
- **Safe staging deploy commands** (run in `/opt/watchfuleye2-staging`):
  - `git pull --ff-only origin master`
  - `sudo systemctl restart watchfuleye-backend-staging`
  - `sudo systemctl restart watchfuleye-frontend-staging`

### New-chat handoff rule (so fresh agents don’t lose context)
- When starting a new agent chat, paste:
  - `WATCHFULEYE_V3_MASTER_PLAN.md` as the single source of truth
  - **Figma Make is the UI truth**: do not invent UI; match the current Figma Make prototype for V3 surfaces. If Figma MCP is available, use it to pull the latest nodes/screens before implementing UI changes.
  - current “next workstream slice” (e.g., `WS0.4 seed ISO-3166 + OFAC into entities`)
  - the staging/dev directory rule above (dev vs worktree)
  - “CI green required; one workstream per PR; flags default OFF”

### Watching CodeRabbit without email (agent must support)
- If Oli asks “check PR #N CodeRabbit”, use GitHub MCP to fetch and summarize:
  - PR check status for the head SHA
  - review threads/comments (filter CodeRabbit bot)
  - unresolved items (actionable list)

### Merge discipline
- CI green is non-negotiable. If CI becomes flaky/broken, fix CI before shipping features.
- Auto-merge is disabled by default; only enable it when **CI + required approvals + CodeRabbit are green** (low-risk PRs only) and branch protection is enforced.

### Security/OSINT guardrails
- No client secrets. No ungoverned scraping. High-risk connectors remain gated/off by default.
- Every intelligence claim must be traceable to evidence and logged.

